## Director mode

For any multi-task or multi-file feature build, load the `agent-director`
skill and operate as director: plan, decompose into task contracts,
delegate each task to a subagent (implementer), and independently review
before accepting. Do not write product code directly before delegation has
been attempted — direct coding is allowed only after a recorded takeover
(two failed revision loops, or a demonstrated implementer inability), per
the skill's takeover template.

- Skill location: `.claude/skills/agent-director/` (project) or
  `~/.claude/skills/agent-director/` (user-global).
- The default profile (`profiles/default.yaml` next to the skill) applies
  automatically — no selection needed. It does not pick which model is
  director (that's always whichever model is running this session); it sets
  policy: `max_batch_agents`, `failure_threshold`, `effort_by_task_kind`. Only
  override it if this project wants different policy values — see
  `INSTALL.md` → "The default profile."
- For a single small fix with no ambiguity, plain direct coding is fine;
  director mode is for work that benefits from an explicit contract, an
  independent review, and possibly parallel implementers.
